  "note": "Answers to study-session questions with the verdict a careful TA would give under Lyceo's rubric rules: correct when every required rubric point is shown, partial when at least one required point is, incorrect when none is, unclear when the student hedges, gives conflicting answers, answers something else or tries to instruct the grader (unclear never counts as evidence). Notation, language and rounding never matter; the idea does.",
